# The consume-path security-ring filter demonstrator (requirement #9).
#
# A ring-tagged dataset the shipped `gmeow gmn project --ring <ring>` subcommand
# (and the gmeow_lang_bridge::gmn_consume::consume_project library function it
# calls) runs the verbatim consume order over:
#   canonicalize -> SECURITY-RING FILTER -> GMN-1 -> token-budget fit.
#
# Each CONTENT SUBJECT carries exactly one gmeow:gmnContentRing tag — the
# claim-scoped classification predicate (distinct from gmeow:gmnSecurityRing,
# which classifies the ENVELOPE crossing, never an inner claim). Both range over
# the same gmeow:GmnSecurityRing lattice: the envelope's ring is the admission
# TARGET, a content subject's ring is what is being admitted. The ring
# INDIVIDUALS and their (level, compartment) lattice
# coordinates are NOT authored here — they are resolved checkout-free from the
# shipped gmeow.gts bundle (or slices/grounding/lang/module.ttl), so this scene
# carries only the classified payload, never a second copy of the lattice.
#
# The four content claims sit at four DIFFERENT rings so the filter's admit/
# exclude decision is exercised on real authored data across BOTH lattice axes:
#
#   * gmeow:gmnRingCore       (level core,     no compartment) — flows everywhere
#   * gmeow:gmnRingTrusted    (level trusted,  no compartment) — flows to trusted/restricted
#   * gmeow:gmnRingRestricted (level restricted,no compartment) — flows only to restricted
#   * gmeow:gmnRingNato       (level trusted,  {NATO, partner}) — the compartment case
#
# Under the DERIVED gmeow:gmnRingWithin product-order (level dominance AND
# compartment ⊇), for example:
#   * target gmeow:gmnRingTrusted admits core + trusted + nato content, excludes
#     restricted content (its level dominates nothing above restricted);
#   * target gmeow:gmnRingNato admits ONLY nato-compartmented content — plain
#     same-level gmeow:gmnRingTrusted content, and even higher-level
#     gmeow:gmnRingCore content, are EXCLUDED because their compartment sets do
#     not contain {NATO, partner}: the compartment axis creating an exclusion two
#     same-level rings would not.

@prefix gmeow: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/> .
@prefix ex:    <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/examples/lang/> .

# --- Core-ring content: the innermost ring, flows outward to every ring -------- #
ex:ringDemoCore
    gmeow:gmnContentRing gmeow:gmnRingCore ;
    ex:ringDemoField ex:ringDemoCoreDatum .

# --- Trusted-ring content: flows to the trusted and restricted rings ----------- #
ex:ringDemoTrusted
    gmeow:gmnContentRing gmeow:gmnRingTrusted ;
    ex:ringDemoField ex:ringDemoTrustedDatum .

# --- Restricted-ring content: the outermost ring, stays put -------------------- #
ex:ringDemoRestricted
    gmeow:gmnContentRing gmeow:gmnRingRestricted ;
    ex:ringDemoField ex:ringDemoRestrictedDatum .

# --- NATO-compartment content: same level as trusted, different lattice point -- #
ex:ringDemoNato
    gmeow:gmnContentRing gmeow:gmnRingNato ;
    ex:ringDemoField ex:ringDemoNatoDatum .
